  "topography": {
    "project_purpose": "RociFi is a decentralized lending protocol that enables undercollateralized loans using on-chain credit scoring. It allows borrowers to access credit based on their reputation and collateral, while lenders provide liquidity to earn yield.",
    "relationship_narrative": "The RociFi V2 family uses a modular architecture where LoanManager orchestrates loan operations, relying on CollateralManager for collateral handling, LimitManager for credit limits, ScoreDB for credit scores, and PriceFeed for asset prices. Pools hold lender funds, and Liquidator handles defaults, all governed by SettingsProvider and access-controlled via NFCS and NamedNFT.",
